        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Every ONE+ battery fits every ONE+ tool, across three chemistries and nearly thirty years, and that promise is the main reason to stay on the platform once you own a few packs. Check the badge on both the tool and the battery, because Ryobi's 40V outdoor line is entirely separate and is the mix-up people actually make.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Where the promise stops is performance. A pack that fits may not deliver the current a brushless chainsaw or circular saw demands, and the tool will bog down or shut off rather than complain. Buy HP packs from now on regardless of what tools you own today, keep the tired old ones for the work light and the inflator, and buy bare tools once you have three or four good batteries.
          </p>
